Subject: Cantor SJS Compiled Lookahead Repository Candidate Extraction P0 Threat Review

& [Threats]
  + locator traversal or platform aliasing falsely presents foreign material as repository local
  + nonauthority evidence claims mandatory coverage and silently becomes governance
  + supplied metrics or edges are changed after digest sealing
  + candidate identity collision obscures element lineage
  + projected-byte or token account understates context cost
  + extraction success is misreported as observed repository truth semantic correctness prompt activation or speedup
  + downstream selector request differs from the one retained in the extraction envelope
  + unknown duplicate or noncanonical JSON fields bypass strict validation

& [Controls]
  + closed enums exact digests portable locator grammar unique identities complete relation validation canonical round trip compositional replay independent verifier and explicit nonauthority
